-## 8. Monitoring & Metrics
+## 8. Rate Limiting Configuration
+
+The gateway applies a global per-client-IP rate limit before routing requests.
+Configure it in `config/gateway.conf` with these keys:
+
+```conf
+rate_limit_enabled = true
+rate_limit_requests = 100
+rate_limit_window_seconds = 60
+```
+
+| Key | Type | Description |
+|-----|------|-------------|
+| `rate_limit_enabled` | `true`/`false` | Enables or disables rate limiting globally. |
+| `rate_limit_requests` | integer | Number of requests allowed from one client IP during the window. |
+| `rate_limit_window_seconds` | integer | Length of the rate-limit window in seconds. |
+
+When the limit is exceeded, the gateway returns HTTP `429` with a JSON error
+response. If the config file or a value is missing, the gateway keeps the
+default of `100` requests per `60` seconds.
+
